From: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
Subject: [PATCH] t20: adapt the frame-channel queue_setup to the 7.x vb2 ABI

frame_channel_vb2_queue_setup() still had the old signature with the
leading const struct v4l2_format *fmt and the trailing alloc_ctxs[]
array.  Since 7.x the callback is

    queue_setup(q, nbuffers, nplanes, sizes, alloc_devs)

so the driver read sizes/alloc_ctxs from the wrong registers/stack slots:
the 6th argument was caller stack garbage and alloc_ctxs[0] wrote
vdev->vbm to a bogus address.  With the framesource now reaching buffer
allocation this caused:

    Unhandled kernel unaligned access, BadVA 0x1
    epc frame_channel_vb2_queue_setup+0x20

Match the 7.x signature and stop filling alloc_devs with the custom vbm
pointer; the custom memops get it from vb2_get_drv_priv().

Signed-off-by: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
---
--- a/driver/t20/sdk/source/tx-isp-frame-channel.c
+++ b/driver/t20/sdk/source/tx-isp-frame-channel.c
@@ -71,9 +71,9 @@
 	return 0;
 }
 
-static int frame_channel_vb2_queue_setup(struct vb2_queue *vq, const struct v4l2_format *fmt,
-			unsigned int *nbuffers, unsigned int *nplanes, unsigned int sizes[],
-			void *alloc_ctxs[])
+static int frame_channel_vb2_queue_setup(struct vb2_queue *vq,
+			unsigned int *nbuffers, unsigned int *nplanes,
+			unsigned int sizes[], struct device *alloc_devs[])
 {
 	frame_chan_vdev_t *vdev = vb2_get_drv_priv(vq);
 	struct frame_channel_attribute *attr = &vdev->attr;
@@ -90,7 +90,12 @@
 
 	*nplanes = 1;
 	sizes[0] = size;
-	alloc_ctxs[0] = vdev->vbm;
+	/*
+	 * The custom memops get vdev->vbm through vb2_get_drv_priv(); the
+	 * 7.x alloc_devs array is only used by the generic DMA memops.
+	 */
+	if (alloc_devs)
+		alloc_devs[0] = NULL;
 
 //	printk("~~~~~~~~ %s[%d] size = %d ~~~~~~~~~~\n",__func__,__LINE__,size);
 	INIT_LIST_HEAD(&vdev->active_list);
